{"id": "DfURhy4vS1B", "title": "Video by feartalkies", "description": "BLINDED BY LOVE | The Wife, the Lover and the Husband. \n\nHere is the complete, unfiltered breakdown of a romance that gripped an entire city. Set in prosperous Visala, a remarkably beautiful young woman named Anangamanjari was bound in marriage to Manivarman, but because she was her father's only child, she remained in her family home while her husband lived elsewhere. While Anangamanjari deeply resented her marriage and found her husband repulsive, Manivarman remained completely devoted to her before eventually leaving on a long journey to visit his parents in Tamralipti.\n\nThe true psychological drama unfolded when Anangamanjari spotted a handsome young man named Kamalakara passing by her window, triggering an instant and overwhelming love at first sight for both. Trapped by rigid societal structures and feeling completely helpless, she believed she could never be with her true love, leading her to sneak into her garden at night to end her life. Fortunately, her loyal confidante discovered her, cut her down, and promised a way to unite them. Yet, when the lovers finally met in secret, the sheer emotional intensity and overwhelming joy proved too much for her fragile state, causing her to collapse and pass away on the spot—setting off a devastating triple tragedy where both the heartbroken lover and the devoted husband also lost their lives to grief.\n\nViewers often wonder why she didn't just walk away or how an emotional reunion could turn fatal. In historical and classical contexts, strict societal constraints made escaping a binding marriage nearly impossible, while extreme emotional spikes whether profound grief or sudden, overwhelming joy frequently triggered fatal physiological shock. Now that you know the complete, unbroken chain of events behind this heartbreaking emotional dilemma, the ultimate question remains: between the wife, the lover, and the husband, whose tragic end or inten